Without delay.
This Bhagavata Purana, while completely rejecting all religious actions inspired by material causes, propounds the supreme truth, which is completely pure
for the devotees with pure hearts. This supreme truth is reality, which, being separate from Maya,
is for the welfare of all. Such truth is the one that completely destroys all three types of suffering. This beautiful Bhagavata, compiled by the great sage Vyasa (in his mature age), is sufficient in itself for the realization of God. So then, what is the need for any other
scripture? As someone carefully and humbly listens to the message of Bhagwat,
God is established in their heart through this ritual of knowledge (anushilan). Meaning: Religion includes four basic subjects-- meritorious deeds, economic development, sensual gratification,
and liberation from worldly bondage. A life of irreverence is a brutal state. In fact, the beginning of human life
begins with the introduction of religion.
Food, sleep, fear and sexual intercourse—these are the four pillars of animal life. These are equally applicable to all four animals and to humans. But in humans, there is an
extra function, religion. Without religion, human life is not better than animal life.
